// Repro (2026-11-19): a pedal bracket whose release is an empty chord at the very end of the piece ('<>@!sustain' as the
// last thing, or 'repeat tremolo N { ... }@!sustain' in the last bar, which reads the same) is not drawn at all.
// With one more bar after it, the bracket is drawn and closes at that bar's head. LilyPond draws it to the final barline.
// Same with the Release lysc of 2026-11-18 and with 145df3333.
// The real case (Kuecken Op.47-3 bar 66, left hand) as the last bar:
//   <fis fis,>16@stemDown@sustain <fis b>64[ dis'64 <fis b>64 dis'64] { <fis b>64[ dis'64 <fis b>64 dis'64] } % % % repeat tremolo 12 { <fis b>64 dis'64 }@!sustain |
octave absolute
time 6/8
part lh { clef bass }

section A {
  lh {
    fis4.@sustain b4. <>@!sustain |
  }
}

score { staff lh }